<script>
  import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.pulse';
  import Footer from '../../components/Footer.pulse';

  let title = "Pulse v0.13.0 Released";
  let subtitle = "The Performance Update: Path Walkers, Template Hoisting, and Keyed Reconciliation.";
  let date = "January 25, 2026";


</script>


lojjojo

<Navbar />

<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <div class="header">
      <span class="date">{date}</span>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">{subtitle}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Pulse v0.13.0 marks a significant milestone in our journey to build a framework that is both simple to use 
        and incredibly performant. This release introduces a completely rewritten hydration and reconciliation engine, 
        inspired by the state-of-the-art techniques used in frameworks like SolidJS.
      </p>

      <h2>The "Path Walker" Strategy</h2>
      <p>
        Traditional frameworks often rely on <code>querySelector</code> or costly Virtual DOM diffing to locate dynamic 
        elements in the page. In v0.13.0, Pulse implements a "Path Walker" (or "Treasure Map") technique.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because Pulse compiles your templates, it knows exactly where the dynamic parts are at build time. 
        Instead of searching for elements at runtime, we now generate a precise map of instructions to walk directly to the target node.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <strong>Comparison:</strong>
        <code>
// Old Way (Searching)
el.querySelector('[data-id="123"]');

// New Way (Walking)
// Path: [0, 1] (First child, then next sibling)
getTargets(root, [[0, 1]]);
        </code>
      </div>

      <h2>Template Hoisting</h2>
      <p>
        We've also introduced Template Hoisting. Static parts of your component are now extracted into 
        <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> elements and created only once. When a component re-renders, we simply clone 
        the template, which is much faster than creating elements one by one using JavaScript.
      </p>

      <h2>Keyed Reconciliation</h2>
      <p>
        The <code>&lt;List&gt;</code> primitive has been upgraded with a Keyed Reconciliation algorithm. 
        Previously, updating a list often meant re-rendering strict parts of it. Now, Pulse intelligently moves 
        existing DOM nodes when the data order changes, minimizing destructive DOM operations and preserving state.
      </p>

      <h2>Stability Improvements</h2>
      <p>
        Along with performance, v0.13.0 addresses critical stability issues found in interactive applications:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Event Bindings:</strong> Fixed a mismatch between server-generated handlers and client-side delegation.</li>
        <li><strong>Reactive Primitives:</strong> ensured <code>&lt;Show&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;List&gt;</code> correctly track signal dependencies in all contexts.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>v0.12.0 vs v0.13.0 Comparison</h2>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Feature</th>
              <th>v0.12.0</th>
              <th>v0.13.0</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>DOM Traversal</strong></td>
              <td>querySelector (Slow)</td>
              <td>Path Walker (O(1))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Template Creation</strong></td>
              <td>Per-Instance</td>
              <td>Hoisted (Clone Node)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>List Updates</strong></td>
              <td>Index-based</td>
              <td>Keyed Reconciliation</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td><strong>Event Delegation</strong></td>
              <td>Partial Support</td>
              <td>Full (data-on-*)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Summary of Changes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Optimization:</strong> Implemented Integer-based Path Walker for O(1) node location.</li>
        <li><strong>Optimization:</strong> Added Template Hoisting to reduce memory and instantiation costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Optimization:</strong> Keyed Reconciliation for efficient List updates.</li>
        <li><strong>Runtime:</strong> Removed `eval()` calls for a more secure and CSP-friendly runtime.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        These changes bring Pulse's performance closer to bare-metal DOM manipulations while keeping the developer 
        experience smooth and reactive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<Footer />

